R2 on the top-20 DE genes.\n\nDataset Information:\n{\n  \"dataset_path\": \"/Users/andresarriaga/Documents/Mila/Gene-Mila/cellforge_runs/cf_norman_s0/data/datasets/norman/norman.h5ad\",\n  \"dataset_name\": \"norman\",\n  \"data_type\": \"scRNA-seq\",\n  \"cell_line\": \"K562\",\n  \"perturbation_type\": \"CRISPRi\"\n}\n\nRelevant Literature:\n- Figure 2\u2014figure supplement 2. Inter-species variability in read counts is greater than intra-species variability.: Figure 2\u2014figure supplement 2. Inter-species variability in read counts is greater than intra-species variability....\n- Figure 8. Gene expression patterns of layer-specific transcription factors.: Figure 8. Gene expression patterns of layer-specific transcription factors....\n- 4703005 Expression vector carrying a gene coding for a phosphate-binding protein, a method for preparing the same and a method for preparing the same and a method for producing a polypeptide using the same: 4703005 Expression vector carrying a gene coding for a phosphate-binding protein, a method for preparing the same and a method for preparing the same and a method for producing a polypeptide using the...\n- Supplementary file 3. CRISPR screen gene-level analysis.: Supplementary file 3. CRISPR screen gene-level analysis....\n- Figure 1\u2014figure supplement 3. GRO-seq signal within protein coding genes is highly correlated between replicates.: Figure 1\u2014figure supplement 3. GRO-seq signal within protein coding genes is highly correlated between replicates....\n\nPlease provide a comprehensive assessment in the following JSON format:\n{\n    \"baseline_models\": {\n        \"literature_review\": {\n            \"existing_methods\": {\n                \"methods\": [\"string\"],\n                \"strengths\": [\"string\"],\n                \"limitations\": [\"string\"],\n                \"biological_relevance\": \"string\"\n            },\n            \"model_comparison\": {\n                \"comparison_criteria\": [\"str