ed terms.\",\n      \"Review prior work and identify the evidence gap, including relevant datasets or theoretical baselines.\",\n      \"Select an appropriate study design: experimental, observational, computational, theoretical, or a combination.\",\n      \"Define data collection or simulation, preprocessing, validation, and quality-control procedures.\",\n      \"Choose statistical or analytical methods and pre-specify decision criteria, including effect sizes or uncertainty thresholds where possible.\",\n      \"Conduct robustness, sensitivity, and alternative-specification checks.\",\n      \"Interpret results, document uncertainty and limitations, and evaluate whether the evidence supports, refutes, or is inconclusive for the hypothesis.\"\n    ],\n    \"success_criteria\": {\n      \"question_clarity\": \"The research question is specific, falsifiable, and relevant to the domain.\",\n      \"input_validity\": \"The problem statement and study details are parseable and unambiguous.\",\n      \"feasibility\": \"A realistic data collection, simulation, or analysis path is identified within stated constraints.\",\n      \"assumption_transparency\": \"All material assumptions are explicitly documented and testable where possible.\",\n      \"reproducibility\": \"Methods, data, code, and environment are sufficient for independent replication.\",\n      \"actionability\": \"Findings can inform decisions, further research, or model refinement.\",\n      \"uncertainty_quantification\": \"Main estimates are reported with appropriate uncertainty measures and sensitivity checks.\"\n    },\n    \"risks_and_limitations\": [\n      \"The framework is domain-agnostic and may not match the true domain-specific problem once details are available.\",\n      \"A parse error may have hidden task-specific details; resubmission in a valid format is required to reduce this risk.\",\n      \"Missing constraints may produce an initial plan that is infeasible in practice.\",\n      \"U